== The Reasons of the Point

#strong[Now I will come to the reasons of the point, and so draw to a close, etc.]

The first #emph[reason] is, that the saints’ hearts may be kept in a humble, praying,#footnote[The philosopher held a ball of brass in his hand; if he happened to fall asleep with it, its fall into a basin woke him to his studies. You are wise, and know how to apply it.] watching frame. Oh, has Satan so many devices to ensnare and ruin the souls of men? How this should awaken dull, drowsy souls, and make them stand on their watch! A saint should be like a #emph[seraph,] covered all over with eyes and lights, so that he may avoid Satan’s snares and stand firm in the hour of temptation. The Lord has revealed in the Scripture the various snares, plots, and devices that the devil has to ruin the souls of men, so that, being forewarned, they may be forearmed, and may always be on their watchtower, holding their weapons in their hands, as the Jews did in Nehemiah’s time, etc.

The second #emph[reason] is, from the malice, envy, and enmity that is in Satan#footnote[Malice does not care what it says or does, so long as it may kill or gall.] against the souls of men. Satan is full of envy and enmity, and that makes him very diligent to suit his snares and plots to the temperaments, constitutions, fancies, and callings of men, so that he may make them as miserable as himself. The Russians are so malicious that a man will hide some of his own goods in the house of the man he hates, and then accuse him of stealing them. So Satan, out of malice to#footnote[An envious heart and a plotting head are inseparable companions.] the souls of men, hides his goods, his wares, as I may say, in the souls of men, and then goes and accuses them before the Lord. And Satan’s malice, envy, and enmity drive him to a thousand thousand other ways to ruin the precious souls of men eternally, etc.

The third #emph[reason] is drawn from the long #emph[experience] that Satan has had. He is a spirit of mighty abilities, and his abilities to lay snares before us are mightily increased by his long standing. He is a spirit of more than five thousand years’ standing. He has had time enough to study all the ways and methods that most tend to ensnare and ruin the souls of men. And as he has had time enough, so he has made it his whole aim, his only aim, his constant aim, to find out snares, depths, and stratagems to entangle and overthrow the souls of men. When he was only a young serpent, he easily deceived and outwitted our first parents; but now he has grown into that #emph[old serpent,] as#footnote[Gen 3.] John speaks. #emph[He is as old as the world,]#footnote[Rev 12:9.] and has grown very cunning by experience.

The fourth #emph[reason] is, in judgment on the men of the world, that they may stumble, and fall, and be ensnared forever. Wicked men who withstand the offers of mercy and despise the Spirit of grace, who will not open, however hard God knocks by his word and rod, by his Spirit and conscience, are given up by a hand of justice to be#footnote[1 Kgs 22:22.] hardened, deceived, and ensnared by Satan to their everlasting ruin. And what can be more just than that they should be taken and charmed by Satan’s wiles, who have often refused to be charmed by the Spirit of grace, though he has charmed ever so wisely and ever so sweetly, etc.?

The fifth #emph[reason] is, that the excellence and power of God’s grace may be the more displayed and made known, by making man able to grapple with this mighty adversary; and that, notwithstanding all the plots, devices, and stratagems of Satan, God will make his people victorious here and crown them with glory hereafter. The greater and more cunning the enemies of the children of Israel were, the more God’s power, wisdom, and goodness sparkled and shone, in that, notwithstanding all their power, plots, and stratagems, etc., he would bring them to Canaan at last. When Paul had well weighed this, #emph[he sits down and glories in his infirmities,]#footnote[2 Cor 12:7, 8, 9.] #emph[and distresses, and Satan’s buffetings, so that the power of Christ might rest on him.]
